{
  "_doc": "Tier-3 grange hall on Church Lane (Pell's Crossing, lot 'grange', front faces the lane): the town's last shelter. Massing (ADR-0021): the main hall rises two storeys open to the roof timbers inside a U of balcony gallery (the old upstairs corridor, with side galleries along both long walls); the lodge room over the stage is the sick bay, with the records room and the Grange master's room beside it, all looking down on the hall. Route: front doors barricaded from inside -> round the side to the kicked-in stage door -> Harold's office (shelter log, records key) -> the stage -> the main hall of cots (a bottle chime across the aisle wakes them) -> the main stair is barricaded -> the kitchen triage station -> the nurses' service stair up -> the nurses' station (ward chart) -> the sick bay (ambush on entry) -> the Grange master's room: the records door (key; alarm on the frame) -> records room (loot: the Grange safe, Harold) -> unbolt the fire door onto the balcony -> drop through its rotten boards to the porch. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
