      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "The Cordon posted notices on every door in Pell's Crossing: assemble at the Grange for evacuation, one bag each, the sick to travel separately. Grange Master Harold Sorensen opened the hall, set out sixty-four cots and the relief crates, and waited for buses that never came. When the fever started he moved the sick upstairs into the old lodge room, barricaded the main stair behind them and let the nurses use the service stair from the kitchen. He locked the county lists, the cash and the last of the antifungals in the records room. Then cot 23 woke up in the dark. The families barricaded the front doors from inside against what was out there, and found out it was already in here with them. Nobody came out the front.",
